---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Lala | She Who Remembers"
  description="The woman holding She Who Remembers: a coaching philosophy of inner authority, embodiment, and discernment, without guru culture or borrowed certainty."
>
  <Hero
    heading="About Lala"
    lede="I hold this work for women who are ready to hear themselves more clearly, not become someone else."
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      This is not an identity you are meant to copy. It is a practice of returning women to
      their own inner vote, so inner authority does not have to be outsourced in order to feel
      supported.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Why I do this work">
        <p>Not as a rescue. As a place where lived experience can become usable wisdom.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I work with women who are remembering how to consult themselves: body, intuition,
          discernment, and action in the same room, instead of in separate compartments that
          never speak.
        </p>
        <p>
          The aim is not to make my voice the one that stays. It is to make a space honest
          enough that a woman can hear her own, including the parts she learned to keep quiet
          in order to remain easy to love.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="A little more human">
        <p>Temperament, not a résumé.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I do not expect people to arrive polished. I do not arrive that way either.</p>
        <p>
          I care about truth, but not the performance of it. Depth, but not heaviness for its
          own sake. Spirituality, but not at the expense of common sense.
        </p>
        <p>
          Serious inner work can include laughter, contradiction, bad timing, a useful insight,
          and the occasional realization that something has become much harder than it needed
          to be. The room can be sacred without becoming solemn.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container>
      <SectionIntro heading="My role">
        <p>Four stances. None of them require you to make me larger than your own knowing.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="role-grid">
        <Card>
          <h3>Mirror</h3>
          <p>
            To reflect what is present, including contradiction, delay, and the pattern that has
            become so fluent it looks like personality.
          </p>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <h3>Midwife</h3>
          <p>
            To support what is already trying to emerge. Not to implant a new self, and not to
            drag a woman into a version of her life she has not chosen.
          </p>
        </Card>
        <Card variant="blush">
          <h3>Sanctuary</h3>
          <p>
            A place where you do not have to perform insight, softness, or healing in order to
            be taken seriously.
          </p>
        </Card>
        <Card variant="blush">
          <h3>Forge</h3>
          <p>
            A place where truth is not endlessly protected from discomfort. Kindness without
            challenge is not the same as care.
          </p>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What I pay attention to">
        <p>Not omniscience. Attention. The difference matters.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ul class="fit">
        <li>What is being said, and what is being said instead of the thing underneath it.</li>
        <li>What is repeatedly avoided, including by intelligence and humor.</li>
        <li>Where language and behavior disagree.</li>
        <li>What the body is signaling before the sentence arrives.</li>
        <li>What belongs to conditioning, loyalty, or an old job in the family.</li>
        <li>What the woman already knows and has not yet been willing to keep.</li>
        <li>Where responsibility actually sits, and where it has been borrowed or dumped.</li>
        <li>What is no longer true, even if it still functions.</li>
        <li>What is asking to be chosen now, in a scale the life can hold.</li>
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What I believe">
        <p>Wholeness is not a costume change.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ul class="beliefs">
        <li>You can be powerful without becoming hard.</li>
        <li>Soft without becoming passive.</li>
        <li>Intuitive without becoming irrational.</li>
        <li>Spiritual without abandoning discernment.</li>
        <li>Loving without abandoning yourself.</li>
        <li>Supported without surrendering authority.</li>
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What I do not believe">
        <p>A short list, because the work is easier to trust when the refusals are named.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ul class="not">
        <li>That a guide should become the center of a woman's spiritual life.</li>
        <li>That dependency is devotion, or that endless access is care.</li>
        <li>That vulnerability has to be performed in order to count.</li>
        <li>That spiritual language can be used to skip the ordinary work of choice.</li>
        <li>That femininity is a performance of softness, desirability, or submission.</li>
        <li>That family is a permanent defendant, or that blame is the same as understanding.</li>
        <li>That every emotion is an instruction. Feeling is information. It still needs discernment.</li>
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Professional scope">
        <p>Coaching and educational work have a job. They do not have every job.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This work does not replace psychotherapy, psychiatric care, medical care, legal
          advice, or crisis services. When those are needed, they are needed. Naming the limit
          is part of respect, not a disclaimer pasted on afterward.
        </p>
      </div>
      <PullQuote>
        Support should return you to yourself. If it slowly replaces you, it is not support.
      </PullQuote>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If you want to see how the work is held"
    primary={{ label: 'Explore the Work', href: withBase('/the-work') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Book a Conversation', href: withBase('/book-a-conversation') }}
  >
    <p>
      The path is the map. A conversation is for the season you are actually in.
    </p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .fit,
  .not,
  .beliefs {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .fit li,
  .not li {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .fit li:last-child,
  .not li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .fit li::before,
  .not li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.7em;
    width: 0.4rem;
    height: 0.4rem;
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .beliefs {
    font-size: var(--text-quote);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: var(--leading-heading);
  }

  .beliefs li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .role-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .role-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .role-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
